$FG,5$$TX+CX,"Selassie Lectures — Scaffold Notes"$$FG$

This directory will hold the public addresses of Haile Selassie I,
formatted as DolDoc and indexed from ::/Doc/Selassie.DD.

$FG,2$Planned contents (Phase 5):$FG$

  WarUN1963.DD       1963 address to the United Nations General
                     Assembly. The "until the philosophy which holds
                     one race superior and another inferior" address.

  OAU1963.DD         1963 Addis Ababa address founding the
                     Organisation of African Unity.

  LeagueOfNations1936.DD
                     1936 address to the League of Nations after the
                     Italian invasion. "It is us today. It will be
                     you tomorrow."

  Jamaica1968.DD     1968 Jamaica state visit remarks.

  Education1967.DD   1967 "Importance of Education" address.

$FG,2$Sourcing:$FG$

  All entries are historical public addresses, transcribed from
  contemporaneous records. Each .DD file leads with a header citing
  the date, venue, and source of the transcription.

$FG,2$Framing:$FG$

  Selassie I identified as Ethiopian Orthodox and did not claim
  divinity. These are presented as the teachings of a head of state
  and reformer, held in reverence by Rastafari, not as scripture.
  See ::/Adam/Jah/JSNotes.DD.
